  "Letta Filesystem gives an agent file tools (grep, search_files, open, close), and a simple GPT-4o mini agent using it scored 74.0% on LoCoMo, above Mem0's reported 68.5% for its top graph variant.": 1,
  "Letta's explanation for the filesystem result is that agents are effective with tools likely in their training data, and iterative self-generated queries beat specialized memory tools designed for single-hop retrieval; agent capability to use a retrieval tool matters more than the retrieval mechanism.": 1,
  "MemGPT introduced memory management for agents via a memory hierarchy inspired by a traditional OS: agents actively manage what stays in immediate context (core memory) versus external layers (conversational memory, archival memory, external files) retrieved as needed.": 1
